    <h1>Privacy Policy – Mini-Games</h1>
    <p><strong>Last updated: May 2026</strong></p>

    <p>Mini-Games (mini-games.ch) respects the privacy of its users. This policy explains what data is collected, how it
        is used, and what rights you have.</p>

    <h2>1. Data Collection</h2>
    <p>Mini-Games does not collect any personally identifiable data. No registration, user accounts, or personal
        information are required.</p>

    <h2>2. Technical Data</h2>
    <p>Certain non-personal data may be collected automatically:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>device type</li>
        <li>browser version</li>
        <li>system language</li>
        <li>anonymous usage statistics</li>
    </ul>
    <p>This data is used solely to ensure the website functions correctly and to improve the user experience.</p>

    <h2>3. Cookies</h2>
    <p>Mini-Games uses technical cookies for the games to function. In addition, third-party cookies may be placed by
        our advertising partners to deliver relevant ads and measure advertising performance.</p>

    <h2>4. Advertisements</h2>
    <p>To keep our services free, Mini-Games displays advertisements provided by third-party networks, such as Adsterra.
        These networks may collect and use non-identifiable data (such as your IP address or your device's advertising
        identifier, such as AAID or IDFA) to personalize ads.</p>

    <h2>5. Data Sharing</h2>
    <p>We do not sell your data. However, non-personal technical information (Advertising ID, device type) is shared
        with our advertising partners (Adsterra) to enable the operation and measurement of advertising campaigns.</p>

    <h2>6. Security</h2>
    <p>We implement technical measures to protect the site and the anonymous data collected.</p>

    <h2>7. Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>Mini-Games may use technical services such as:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>web hosting</li>
        <li>anonymized performance tools</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>8. Children</h2>
    <p>Mini-Games is intended for a general audience. No personal data is collected from children.</p>

    <h2>9. Contact</h2>
    <p>For any questions regarding this policy:<br>
        <a href="mailto:contact@mini-games.ch">contact@mini-games.ch</a>
    </p>

    <h2>10. Changes</h2>
    <p>This policy may be updated. The most recent version is always available on this page.</p>

